Ending_01
[background arg="res://assets/cg/Endings/end01.png" fade="0.0"]
Narrator: After understanding Marloch's history. Catherine wants to live but doesn’t want to give up on Marloch. She also ends up resenting humanity’s greed.
Narrator: Marloch and Catherine reach an agreement where Marloch turns Catherine into a magical creature and Catherine ends up living with Marloch in the magical realm.
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/Forest_placeHolder.jpg" fade="0.0"]
Narrator: Marloch has told her everything now. The wishes, the losses, the centuries of forgetting himself one grant at a time.
join Marloch center
Marloch: I could cure you. Or... I could give you something else. A longer answer than a cure.
catherine: Tell me.
Marloch: Become like me. No sickness, no clock running out  but no home to go back to, either. Not really. Not as you were.
catherine: I stopped wanting to go back the day I understood what "home" cost people like you.
Marloch: Then let's not waste any more of either of our centuries.
Narrator: Catherine becomes a creature of Shateroo's hidden world, and stays there, with Marloch, at the edge of the trees where the two worlds meet.
[signal arg="game_end"]